timeline.body:
bwc nit: if `request#waitForCompletion == false` but we're sending to an older version that doesn't understand this new field then we shouldn't simply drop it like this. Instead it'd be better to check `ClusterState#getMinTransportVersion` in `TransportDeleteSnapshotAction#doExecute` similarly to `org.elasticsearch.action.admin.cluster.allocation.TransportGetAllocationStatsAction#doExecute`, and fail the request if the cluster hasn't been fully upgraded yet. Then we can at least assert that this case doesn't happen here (but ideally also throw something):

```suggestion
        if (out.getTransportVersion().onOrAfter(TransportVersions.DELETE_SNAPSHOTS_ASYNC_ADDED)) {
            out.writeBoolean(waitForCompletion);
        } else {
            assert waitForCompletion;
        }
```

